window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Daniella Thornton is used to disappearing.</b></p> <p>After her husband's death, the doctor is dedicated to guarding her heart and providing the best she can for her hearing-impaired daughter, Emily.</p> <p>But when a charismatic producer named Alex Blackwell steps into the picture and forms an unexpected bond with her daughter, Daniella's heart is threatened once again. Alex is known for throwing lavish parties and breaking hearts. He's the last person Daniella needs in her and her daughter's life.</p> <p>Yet he seems determined to prove himself a changed man, and Daniella can't seem to stay away from him.</p> <p>But Daniella's past tracks her down once again to the shores of Plum Island, and she prepares to make her and her daughter disappear again. This time, though, she's not alone. This time, Alex and Daniella have the chance to free Daniella from her dangerous past and forge a new life.</p> <p>The Library on Plum Island <i>is a story where the sea murmurs long-forgotten secrets and romance blooms throughout a journey of friendship, redemption, and strength. Witness the strength of a small community as it rises to protect one of its own against the shadows of the past.</i></p> <p>The Library on Plum Island <i>is book four of the Cobble Beach Romance series, a powerful, clean and wholesome women's saga in which heartwarming strong characters have a second chance at romance if they believe it is possible and let go of the past. For the best experience listen to the books in order.</i></p>"; 
